Halley on OpenRC
================

Halley is a user-scoped graphical session, so it does not install an OpenRC
system service. Install and start seatd (or elogind) as a system service, then
launch /usr/bin/halley-session from a display manager or login shell.

The session wrapper detects that systemd is not booted and executes Halley
directly. Halley publishes WAYLAND_DISPLAY and its desktop identity to the
D-Bus activation environment after the compositor socket is ready, so portals
and other desktop services work without systemctl.

Set HALLEY_NO_INIT_INTEGRATION=1 to force this direct path even when a supported
user service manager is present.
